      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's really helpful for my section on the \"socialization\" angle. You mentioned that they used these theories to frame it as a \"rational\" way to manage the population. To make my essay more rigorous, I want to explore the specific \"outcomes\" they were trying to optimize for. \n\nIf a policymaker from that era was making a presentation about why segregation was the most efficient way to run a state, how would they have articulated the \"benefits\" of separation in terms of crime rates or economic stability? I'm trying to understand how they used those biological or sociological claims to create a blueprint for a \"stable\" society. Could you expand on how those arguments were structured to show that segregation was a practical tool for public safety?",
